<title>ARGENTINA: Santander downgrades Argentina's Siderca.</title>
<headline>Santander downgrades Argentina's Siderca.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Santander Investment said Wednesday it downgraded Argentine steelmaker Siderca to market perform from buy &quot;because it is fairly valued&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;Since we initiated coverage of the stock on March 12, 1997, the price has risen by 19 percent, owing to its attractive valuation and excellent prospects,&quot; analyst Andres Biolcati said in a report.  </p>
<p>&quot;However, we believe that Siderca's return will be similar to that of the Argentine market going forward, mainly because we believe that the company is fairly valued&quot;, he added.</p>
<p>Siderca, controlled by local industrial holding company Techint, forms an strategic allegiance with Tubos de Acero de Mexico SA (TAMSA) and Italy's Dalmine.</p>
<p>((-Guillermo Haskel, Buenos Aires Newsroom, 541 318-0650))</p>
